      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1962, Tombstone was declared a National Historic Landmark District, preserving its 1870s‑80s frontier atmosphere for future generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Tombstone-Arizona",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Boot Hill in Tombstone is one of the best‑known pioneer cemeteries, where many were buried after “dying with their boots on.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
